implementationPlan.description:
TEST FIRST: DoD 1 and 2. Reference bytes are in /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-fa70e835/ (outside the repo; SHA256SUMS lists every file). The architect ran them RED and GREEN in a snapshot. Copy them with your own editor tool only (Write/Edit on Claude, apply_patch on codex exec), never a shell write (project rail).

Create packages/moe-daemon/src/state/blockedTimeoutPresence.test.ts from blockedTimeoutPresence.test.ts (sha256 77e1347903ba7eb6f58086c47ae59e1c5a86e1e20244cc7143ab844c3af4d588). It uses ToolTestHarness, but swaps in a StateManager with explicit blockedTimeoutMs 1 h and staleWorkerTimeoutMs 3 h, so no project.json setting can move either line. Two seats are each parked BLOCKED by a third-party block on an assigned WORKING row (blockedFromStatus WORKING):
- worker-pruned, silent 4 h: past both lines, so it is timed out and then pruned;
- worker-kept, silent 2 h: past blockedTimeoutMs only, so it is timed out and then kept, inside the prune window.
The postToRoleChannel and postToGeneral spies stop chat side effects.

Test 1, 'keeps the real lastActivityAt, so the seat never reads alive, and the same pass prunes the one that owns nothing', calls the real checkBlockedTimeouts once and asserts:
- both rows are parked to BACKLOG, unassigned (the documented park is unchanged);
- worker-kept matches { status: 'IDLE', currentTaskId: null, lastError: null, lastActivityAt: its pre-sweep value } and isWorkerAlive(record) is false (DoD 1);
- getWorker('worker-pruned') is null: Layer 3 of the same pass removed it (DoD 2);
- after flushActivityLog, the worker's own WORKER_TIMEOUT entry (workerId worker-kept, no taskId) still exists, and its payload carries the preserved lastActivityAt.

Test 2, 'a daemon restart right after the timeout does not spare the timed-out seat', runs the sweep, then purgeAllWorkers(), and asserts worker-kept is gone. Before the fix it reads as alive, so the purge kept it.

One test holds both seats because a pruned record cannot show its stamp.

RED in a snapshot, never in place (project rail): `S=$(mktemp -d) && git archive HEAD packages/moe-daemon docs scripts CLAUDE.md | tar -x -C "$S"`, cp --parents the new test file into it, then in $S/packages/moe-daemon run `npm ci` and `npx vitest run src/state/blockedTimeoutPresence.test.ts` under the checkRef's env -i PATH (nvm Node 24). Expected: 2 failed. Test 1 fails on lastActivityAt (re-stamped to now) and test 2 fails on 'expected { id: worker-kept … } to be null'.
